{"id":"032ce0ae-b47e-4491-b8c9-fa7fd40bca68","object":"chat.completion","created":1785019324,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    allocations = [seg['minimum'] for seg in segments]\\n    capacities = [seg['capacity'] for seg in segments]\\n    sum_min = sum(allocations)\\n    sum_cap = sum(capacities)\\n    if budget < sum_min or budget > sum_cap:\\n        raise ValueError('Budget infeasible')\\n    remaining = budget - sum_min\\n    # current allocations already at minima\\n    # allocate remaining tokens one by one\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        best_val = -1.0\\n        for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\\n            if allocations[i] < capacities[i]:\\n                # importance divided by next allocated position (current+1)\\n                val = seg['importance'] / (allocations[i] + 1)\\n                if val > best_val:\\n                    best_val = val\\n                    best_idx = i\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            # Should not happen because budget <= total capacity\\n            raise ValueError('Infeasible allocation')\\n        allocations[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    by_name = {seg['name']: allocations[i] for i, seg in enumerate(segments)}\\n    total = sum(allocations)\\n    return {'allocations': allocations, 'by_name': by_name, 'total': total}\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write solve(case) that implements a budget allocation algorithm. The case has segments list with name, importance, minimum, capacity. Also budget. We need to allocate tokens: start with each segment at its minimum. Then while remaining budget > 0, allocate one token to segment that maximizes importance / (next_position) where next_position is current allocation+1? Actually \"importance divided by its next allocated position\" means if segment currently has alloc tokens, next token would be at position alloc+1, so ratio = importance / (alloc+1). We need to break ties by original segment order (index in list). After allocation, we need output: allocations (list of integers in same order as segments? Probably yes, each integer is final allocation for that segment), by_name (object mapping segment name to allocation), total (sum of allocations). Must equal budget exactly if within capacity. If budget < sum of minima, raise ValueError. If budget > sum of capacities, raise ValueError. Also if any segment's minimum > capacity? Possibly but not specified; assume valid.\n\nImplementation details: iterate while budget_left > 0. For each segment, compute candidate = importance / (current_alloc + 1). Find max. If multiple, pick smallest index. Add one to that segment, decrement budget. Ensure not exceed capacity (but we already ensured budget <= total capacity, so okay). Use simple loop.\n\nEdge cases: budget exactly sum minima then no allocation. Also note \"stable_tie_break\" meaning original order.\n\nReturn dictionary with keys \"allocations\", \"by_name\", \"total\". allocations is list of ints. by_name is dict. total is int.\n\nWe must follow strict output schema: by_name has dynamicKeysFrom case.segments[*].name, so okay.\n\nImplementation code: def solve(case): ... then compute.\n\nWe need to return a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the source string.\n\nMake sure to escape properly.\n\nNow write code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1499,"completion_tokens":751,"total_tokens":2250,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1408},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":405},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1408,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":91},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}